      "quality": {
        "is_fragment": false,
        "is_ocr_suspect": false
      },
      "sequence": 1,
      "answer": "According to the text, India has attracted people globally due to several intrinsic cultural values that facilitate inclusion and acceptance:\n\n1.  **Fundamental Human Unity:** There is a core civilisational value of recognizing fundamental unity of humankind, which offers hope to resolve global crises like wars, climate change, inequality, and discrimination.\n\n2.  **Inclusive Values:** Specific values such as *vasudhaiva kutumbakam* (the world is one family), *atithi devo bhava* (a foreign guest is dearer than a born god), and *sarve bhavantu sukhinah* (may all be blessed) are central to the sense of inclusion.\n\n3.  **Historical Sanctuary:** Historically, India has served as a haven for people facing persecution in their own lands or looking for new opportunities.\n\n4.  **Security and Tradition:** For small communities seeking security, these values have allowed them to maintain their traditions while finding a secure place to live over centuries."
    }
  ],
